1
00:00:43,570 --> 00:00:46,590
[Yangju Korea Hospital]

2
00:00:49,257 --> 00:00:51,068
Ma'am! Can you hear me?

3
00:00:51,068 --> 00:00:52,958
Ma'am! Keep pressure on the wound!

4
00:00:52,958 --> 00:00:54,830
Get the red blood cell ready,
and set the blood line to max!

5
00:00:54,830 --> 00:00:56,628
- Ha Na...
- Keep pressing!

6
00:00:56,628 --> 00:00:58,328
Ha Na.

7
00:00:59,804 --> 00:01:01,291
No, you can't come in!

8
00:01:01,291 --> 00:01:02,675
I'm sorry, sir!

9
00:01:02,675 --> 00:01:04,880
I'm so sorry, but you can't come in!

10
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:21,371
The suspect weaved through
the security camera's blind spots,

11
00:01:21,371 --> 00:01:23,708
so he must've done his research
on the exit route.

12
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:28,079
We've got the Coast Guard
searching the ports for any stowaways,

13
00:01:28,079 --> 00:01:32,885
but this seems to have been premeditated.

14
00:01:37,727 --> 00:01:39,564
We're past the immediate crisis,

15
00:01:39,564 --> 00:01:42,341
but she has suffered great blood loss,
and severe brain damage.

16
00:01:42,341 --> 00:01:47,311
We'll have to see if she regains consciousness
and all organ function.

17
00:02:00,329 --> 00:02:02,488
What do we do?

18
00:02:27,127 --> 00:02:28,551
<i>What's this?</i>

19
00:02:28,551 --> 00:02:31,940
<i>Why do you have this, Woo Jae?</i>

20
00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:38,100
<i>I thought you gave it over to Yang Jun Mo.</i>

21
00:02:40,958 --> 00:02:44,203
<i>Of course I wouldn't hand over
the real one to Yang Jun Mo.</i>

22
00:02:46,182 --> 00:02:48,552
<i>You never know what he'd do with it.</i>

23
00:02:48,552 --> 00:02:50,846
<i>I kept the real one.</i>

24
00:02:58,978 --> 00:03:03,199
Ha Na may not ever regain consciousness,

25
00:03:03,199 --> 00:03:07,710
and even if she does,
the chance of a full recovery is...

26
00:03:07,710 --> 00:03:09,410
small.

27
00:03:14,085 --> 00:03:15,924
We've got to find a way.

28
00:03:15,924 --> 00:03:17,624
Whatever it takes.

29
00:03:23,298 --> 00:03:26,258
It's in smithereens. This is beyond repair.

30
00:03:26,258 --> 00:03:27,975
Is there nothing you can do?

31
00:03:27,975 --> 00:03:30,319
This is a very old model, you see.

32
00:03:30,319 --> 00:03:32,509
I can't get the parts for it.

33
00:03:33,118 --> 00:03:35,753
I don't think I can fix this. Here.

34
00:03:39,710 --> 00:03:42,554
It's hard to find parts
for this model nowadays.

35
00:03:42,554 --> 00:03:44,783
We can't fix it, sorry.

36
00:03:44,783 --> 00:03:46,183
This can't be fixed.

37
00:03:46,183 --> 00:03:47,400
What a relic.

38
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:48,525
No way, nope.

39
00:03:48,525 --> 00:03:49,674
This won't do.

40
00:03:49,674 --> 00:03:51,970
It's just too old.

41
00:04:08,391 --> 00:04:10,045
<i>For me,</i>

42
00:04:10,045 --> 00:04:13,618
<i>the fact that I can love you
with everything I have...</i>

43
00:04:13,618 --> 00:04:15,995
<i>just gives me so much joy.</i>

44
00:04:15,995 --> 00:04:17,926
<i>It makes me happy.</i>

45
00:04:17,926 --> 00:04:19,626
<i>Woo Jae.</i>

46
00:04:20,351 --> 00:04:22,051
<i>I love you.</i>

47
00:04:24,218 --> 00:04:26,852
Is the magic gone now?

48
00:04:28,638 --> 00:04:30,202
Why can't I...

49
00:04:30,811 --> 00:04:33,174
save you?

50
00:04:36,525 --> 00:04:39,091
It should've been me, not you.

51
00:04:40,805 --> 00:04:43,206
I should've been the one to save you.

52
00:05:12,751 --> 00:05:14,664
[Episode 12]

53
00:05:19,271 --> 00:05:21,378
What do we do?

54
00:05:22,738 --> 00:05:24,803
Is there nothing else we can do?

55
00:05:25,478 --> 00:05:27,863
Let's ask around a bit more.

56
00:05:32,211 --> 00:05:33,371
Hey.

57
00:05:33,371 --> 00:05:34,783
Give it here.

58
00:05:41,578 --> 00:05:43,215
Who are you?

59
00:05:43,215 --> 00:05:46,318
What's your business?

60
00:05:48,198 --> 00:05:50,338
[We Buy, Sell &amp; Repair]

61
00:05:57,758 --> 00:05:59,548
Hey, is there any chance...

62
00:05:59,548 --> 00:06:02,286
we've met each other somewhere before?

63
00:06:02,286 --> 00:06:04,010
I feel like I could recognize you.

64
00:06:04,010 --> 00:06:05,352
You think?

65
00:06:05,978 --> 00:06:08,780
I don't know. Maybe we passed each other by.

66
00:06:09,525 --> 00:06:11,542
- Okay...
- This thing...

67
00:06:11,542 --> 00:06:13,812
It's on its last life.

68
00:06:13,812 --> 00:06:15,236
- Pardon me?
- Still...

69
00:06:15,236 --> 00:06:18,054
It's got the video you took.
What a relief, right?

70
00:06:18,705 --> 00:06:20,469
I don't understand.

71
00:06:20,469 --> 00:06:22,893
I mean, how did you...

72
00:06:22,893 --> 00:06:26,458
Mister, what are you, exactly?

73
00:06:26,458 --> 00:06:28,840
Wait, you're not... God, are you?

74
00:06:29,951 --> 00:06:31,268
Or an angel?

75
00:06:31,268 --> 00:06:32,523
Me?

76
00:06:34,018 --> 00:06:36,000
They call me a fairy.

77
00:06:42,491 --> 00:06:44,048
A fairy?

78
00:06:50,838 --> 00:06:52,328
Oh, right.

79
00:06:52,328 --> 00:06:53,846
I was wondering,

80
00:06:53,846 --> 00:06:56,716
if we travel back to the past again,

81
00:06:56,716 --> 00:06:59,414
will Woo Jae and I... You know...

82
00:06:59,414 --> 00:07:03,248
Will our bodies... swap again?

83
00:07:03,248 --> 00:07:04,952
Oh, that?

84
00:07:04,952 --> 00:07:06,463
No, that won't happen anymore.

85
00:07:06,463 --> 00:07:08,880
That was an honest mistake, my bad.

86
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:10,038
I see.

87
00:07:10,038 --> 00:07:11,615
A mistake...

88
00:07:11,615 --> 00:07:12,859
A mistake?

89
00:07:12,859 --> 00:07:15,126
Did you just say "a mistake?"

90
00:07:16,191 --> 00:07:17,668
Hey, Mister!

91
00:07:17,668 --> 00:07:21,312
Because of your "honest mistake,"

92
00:07:21,312 --> 00:07:23,158
I had to wear a skirt!

93
00:07:23,158 --> 00:07:24,476
A flappy, breezy skirt!

94
00:07:24,476 --> 00:07:26,151
And don't get me started on the hair!

95
00:07:26,151 --> 00:07:27,875
This bastard confessed to me!

96
00:07:27,875 --> 00:07:29,466
It wasn't for you!

97
00:07:29,466 --> 00:07:31,490
You know what I mean.

98
00:07:31,490 --> 00:07:33,627
I can't even put it into words!

99
00:07:33,627 --> 00:07:35,674
You get me?

100
00:07:35,674 --> 00:07:37,105
You're not perfect, either.

101
00:07:37,105 --> 00:07:38,618
He's got a point.

102
00:07:38,618 --> 00:07:40,029
What?

103
00:07:43,505 --> 00:07:46,216
There you go.

104
00:07:46,216 --> 00:07:47,916
Thank you, sir.

105
00:08:06,403 --> 00:08:08,103
It's on.

106
00:08:10,891 --> 00:08:13,118
No way!

107
00:08:13,118 --> 00:08:14,992
Thank you, Mr. Fairy...

108
00:08:20,918 --> 00:08:22,878
What the...

109
00:08:22,878 --> 00:08:24,899
Was he really a fairy?

110
00:08:25,658 --> 00:08:27,625
That can't be.

111
00:08:27,625 --> 00:08:30,032
His eyes were pretty fairy-like, though.

112
00:08:35,745 --> 00:08:37,445
Thank goodness.

113
00:09:35,631 --> 00:09:38,195
I was feeling down, so I bought a yacht.

114
00:09:38,195 --> 00:09:40,085
How about a yacht party tomorrow?

115
00:09:40,085 --> 00:09:42,413
- Good for you.
- What a shame.

116
00:09:42,413 --> 00:09:44,846
Our chef gets horribly seasick, you see.

117
00:09:44,846 --> 00:09:48,843
Do you know I own a building
at Avenue Montaigne in Paris?

118
00:09:48,843 --> 00:09:51,580
If you want, you can open a restaurant there.

119
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:53,111
I'll deal with all the papers.

120
00:09:53,111 --> 00:09:55,729
How's that? You want to come with me?

121
00:09:55,729 --> 00:09:58,138
Wow, Montaigne, huh?

122
00:09:58,138 --> 00:09:59,935
Now, now.

123
00:09:59,935 --> 00:10:05,383
We already have several offers
under the chef's name.

124
00:10:05,383 --> 00:10:06,454
Okay?

125
00:10:06,454 --> 00:10:09,711
I'll give you my email address,
and you can send me an email there.

126
00:10:09,711 --> 00:10:12,331
I'll run it through and write back.

127
00:10:12,331 --> 00:10:14,072
I will get back to you, okay?

128
00:10:14,072 --> 00:10:16,725
Here's my business card.

129
00:10:16,725 --> 00:10:18,262
Here.

130
00:10:18,262 --> 00:10:20,655
What? The hell are you talking about?

131
00:10:20,655 --> 00:10:22,374
I had it made yesterday.

132
00:10:28,418 --> 00:10:30,808
- Hey, what's wrong?
- What's wrong?

133
00:10:30,808 --> 00:10:32,508
Are you okay?

134
00:10:38,171 --> 00:10:39,931
Are you alright?

135
00:10:39,931 --> 00:10:42,065
- What's wrong?
- What?

136
00:10:42,065 --> 00:10:43,410
Yeah...

137
00:10:49,345 --> 00:10:52,330
<i>I'm back to the day before the award ceremony.</i>

138
00:10:53,618 --> 00:10:55,207
Who is it?

139
00:10:55,921 --> 00:10:57,698
Hey, Gyeong Woo!

140
00:10:57,698 --> 00:10:59,462
I need to get going!

141
00:10:59,462 --> 00:11:01,198
- Have fun!
- Wait, wait!

142
00:11:01,198 --> 00:11:03,177
- Where are you going?
- I'll drive you...

143
00:11:04,034 --> 00:11:05,931
I guess I won't be driving him.

144
00:11:05,931 --> 00:11:08,695
So how about we have some serious talk...

145
00:11:42,538 --> 00:11:44,849
<i>Did I actually make it?</i>

146
00:11:53,218 --> 00:11:55,625
<i>The day before the ceremony...</i>

147
00:11:55,625 --> 00:11:57,041
Ha Na.

148
00:11:58,418 --> 00:12:00,878
Where are you going? Woo Jae!

149
00:12:00,878 --> 00:12:02,390
Hey!

150
00:12:09,062 --> 00:12:11,615
Why is it so quiet in here?

151
00:12:52,891 --> 00:12:54,591
Thank goodness...

152
00:12:56,271 --> 00:12:57,971
I'm so relieved.

153
00:13:07,667 --> 00:13:12,214
So, you and Yoon Ha Na
are shooting Yang Jun Mo's movie?

154
00:13:13,158 --> 00:13:16,425
Yeah, since a week ago.

155
00:13:16,425 --> 00:13:19,518
So, Park Gi Tae, who stabbed me and fled,

156
00:13:19,518 --> 00:13:22,451
and all the evidence that we had... are gone?

157
00:13:22,451 --> 00:13:24,479
And I'm in a coma?

158
00:13:27,287 --> 00:13:28,891
So...

159
00:13:28,891 --> 00:13:31,392
You all came here because of me.

160
00:13:32,465 --> 00:13:34,283
Of course we did.

161
00:13:36,671 --> 00:13:39,538
You guys are like two peas in a pod.

162
00:13:39,538 --> 00:13:42,818
Hey! Both of you, I'm sick of this!

163
00:13:42,818 --> 00:13:44,542
"It's my fault..."

164
00:13:44,542 --> 00:13:45,632
"Because of me..."

165
00:13:45,632 --> 00:13:47,856
Stop saying that! No more moping!

166
00:13:47,856 --> 00:13:49,691
I'm banning you!

167
00:13:49,691 --> 00:13:51,905
Sure, it's because of Woo Jae,
and sometimes it's because of Ha Na.

168
00:13:51,905 --> 00:13:54,325
So what? Let's say it was because of me.

169
00:13:54,325 --> 00:13:57,388
Wouldn't you do the same? To save me?

170
00:14:00,625 --> 00:14:02,135
Of course we would.

171
00:14:02,135 --> 00:14:03,686
Yeah.

172
00:14:03,686 --> 00:14:05,345
See?

173
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:07,589
So please, I'm begging you.

174
00:14:07,589 --> 00:14:09,218
Let's not be overly apologetic to each other.

175
00:14:09,218 --> 00:14:12,915
We're short on time.
We literally don't have time to mope around!

176
00:14:12,915 --> 00:14:14,978
Okay?

177
00:14:14,978 --> 00:14:16,931
- Okay.
- Okay.

178
00:14:16,931 --> 00:14:18,502
Perfect.

179
00:14:21,605 --> 00:14:23,522
Anyway, why did you guys hesitate?

180
00:14:24,208 --> 00:14:26,082
You'll... save me, right?

181
00:14:26,082 --> 00:14:27,488
Right?

182
00:14:30,725 --> 00:14:32,285
Where's Ha Ri?

183
00:14:32,285 --> 00:14:34,166
You should've contacted her sooner.

184
00:14:36,538 --> 00:14:38,071
By the way...

185
00:14:38,071 --> 00:14:40,592
that's not your father, you said?

186
00:14:40,592 --> 00:14:42,275
No, he isn't.

187
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,111
Does he have a twin?

188
00:14:45,111 --> 00:14:47,998
We were thinking of finding out, actually.

189
00:14:47,998 --> 00:14:49,960
A hidden uncle?

190
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:51,265
Some sort of family secret?

191
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:53,925
But Park Gi Tae and Yang Jun Mo come first.

192
00:14:53,925 --> 00:14:55,242
You don't know anything, do you?

193
00:14:55,242 --> 00:14:58,032
- You're such an annoying...
- Our clients.

194
00:14:58,032 --> 00:14:59,876
You're all very famous people, yes?

195
00:14:59,876 --> 00:15:03,738
Oh, we won't ask you
for your signatures or anything.

196
00:15:03,738 --> 00:15:05,902
You can rest easy.

197
00:15:05,902 --> 00:15:08,499
- Our confidentiality policy...
- Must be pretty strict.

198
00:15:08,499 --> 00:15:10,371
What say we rest assured?

199
00:15:10,371 --> 00:15:13,823
Okay. Now, shall we begin?

200
00:15:16,338 --> 00:15:17,712
Good.

201
00:15:54,978 --> 00:15:57,191
<i>We need to secure the evidence</i>

202
00:15:57,191 --> 00:15:58,791
<i>before Yang Jun Mo can get rid of it.</i>

203
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:01,004
<i>First, see that the ceremony ends well.</i>

204
00:16:01,004 --> 00:16:04,282
<i>Just like it happened. Don't change a thing.</i>

205
00:16:05,264 --> 00:16:09,471
<i>Make sure not to let
Yang Jun Mo get suspicious.</i>

206
00:16:09,471 --> 00:16:14,952
<i>The Best Actor Award of the
30th Baekryong Film Awards, 2026, goes to...</i>

207
00:16:14,952 --> 00:16:16,795
<i>Jung Woo Jae, from the movie "Thirties."</i>

208
00:16:16,795 --> 00:16:18,368
<i>Congratulations.</i>

209
00:16:37,431 --> 00:16:41,878
First of all, I thank you all for granting me
such an honorable award.

210
00:16:41,878 --> 00:16:44,132
I won't grow complacent.

211
00:16:44,132 --> 00:16:46,896
I will always be eager to learn,

212
00:16:46,896 --> 00:16:49,303
and to become an honest actor.

213
00:16:50,871 --> 00:16:52,483
Thank you.

214
00:17:35,671 --> 00:17:37,597
Do you like me that much?

215
00:17:43,438 --> 00:17:47,038
Enough to miss me
as soon as you open your eyes?

216
00:17:48,091 --> 00:17:50,094
Stop it.

217
00:17:52,458 --> 00:17:54,931
- You were pretending to be asleep?
- Yeah.

218
00:17:54,931 --> 00:17:56,548
I was.

219
00:17:56,548 --> 00:17:58,248
You...

220
00:18:24,445 --> 00:18:26,472
Everything should stay the same, right?

221
00:18:27,704 --> 00:18:29,168
Stay the same?

222
00:18:29,168 --> 00:18:30,812
With the past.

223
00:18:30,812 --> 00:18:32,584
You said not to change it.

224
00:18:34,611 --> 00:18:36,839
This past is known only to me.

225
00:18:37,611 --> 00:18:39,311
I'll lead you. Just trust me.

226
00:19:06,271 --> 00:19:08,618
Emotional... paralysis?

227
00:19:08,618 --> 00:19:09,676
What's that?

228
00:19:09,676 --> 00:19:14,384
My brain can't process emotions like
happiness, sadness, and even surprise.

229
00:19:14,384 --> 00:19:16,695
It has a delayed response to feelings.

230
00:19:16,695 --> 00:19:19,015
Like an emotional short circuit.

231
00:19:21,185 --> 00:19:22,743
Ha Na.

232
00:19:22,743 --> 00:19:24,769
Are you okay?

233
00:19:24,769 --> 00:19:29,473
<i>My brain can't process emotions like
happiness, sadness, and even surprise.</i>

234
00:19:29,473 --> 00:19:31,482
<i>It has a delayed response to feelings.</i>

235
00:19:31,482 --> 00:19:33,611
<i>Like an emotional short circuit.</i>

236
00:19:33,611 --> 00:19:35,311
Emotional...

237
00:19:36,044 --> 00:19:37,527
paralysis?

238
00:19:45,391 --> 00:19:47,091
I'm sorry, Jun Mo.

239
00:19:47,751 --> 00:19:50,811
- You should get a new actress for the role.
- No.

240
00:19:54,031 --> 00:19:55,555
First things first.

241
00:19:55,555 --> 00:19:57,526
You should focus on recovery.

242
00:19:57,526 --> 00:19:59,850
- Jun Mo.
- It has to be you.

243
00:20:00,605 --> 00:20:04,005
Nobody else will suffice.
Never. It would be pointless.

244
00:20:04,005 --> 00:20:05,815
So empty your mind.

245
00:20:05,815 --> 00:20:07,825
Just focus on yourself.

246
00:20:07,825 --> 00:20:09,525
On your recovery.

247
00:20:10,118 --> 00:20:12,244
I'll wait for however long it takes.

248
00:20:12,831 --> 00:20:14,531
It's fine, really.

249
00:20:16,751 --> 00:20:18,115
Jun Mo.

250
00:20:18,765 --> 00:20:19,811
Yes?

251
00:20:19,811 --> 00:20:24,532
I know how I shine
in the frame that you create.

252
00:20:24,532 --> 00:20:26,726
I know it well.

253
00:20:27,367 --> 00:20:29,598
For that, I am infinitely thankful.

254
00:20:29,598 --> 00:20:31,298
It's an honor.

255
00:20:32,274 --> 00:20:35,002
- You're making me blush.
- However,

256
00:20:35,002 --> 00:20:37,586
your film will shine anyway, even without me.

257
00:20:37,586 --> 00:20:39,223
I, too,

258
00:20:39,223 --> 00:20:41,667
will shine just as brightly without your movie.

259
00:20:41,667 --> 00:20:43,042
Ha Na...

260
00:20:43,669 --> 00:20:46,415
- That's not...
- The world that you create

261
00:20:46,415 --> 00:20:48,912
won't waver without me.

262
00:20:48,912 --> 00:20:50,638
I truly wish with all my heart,

263
00:20:50,638 --> 00:20:54,920
that you become a renowned director
who is loved for a long time.

264
00:21:00,494 --> 00:21:03,754
You don't have to pretend
to be okay in front of me.

265
00:21:03,754 --> 00:21:05,125
Ha Na.

266
00:21:05,125 --> 00:21:07,362
You're the best actress in my eyes.

267
00:21:07,362 --> 00:21:08,973
<i>Whatever anyone else says,</i>

268
00:21:08,973 --> 00:21:11,321
<i>you are the best ever, at least in my life.</i>

269
00:21:11,321 --> 00:21:14,205
<i>You, Ha Na, are the best actress ever,
at least to me.</i>

270
00:21:14,205 --> 00:21:17,154
You'll get better soon. Don't worry.

271
00:21:17,154 --> 00:21:18,627
Understood?

272
00:22:14,401 --> 00:22:16,509
It's begun again.

273
00:22:28,321 --> 00:22:30,683
Ha Na, did you sleep well?

274
00:22:32,285 --> 00:22:33,709
Should we, like...

275
00:22:33,709 --> 00:22:36,040
send it back, or something?

276
00:22:56,941 --> 00:22:58,377
Ha Na!

277
00:22:59,121 --> 00:23:01,721
- Ha Na!
- What, what is it?

278
00:23:01,721 --> 00:23:03,165
What's wrong, Ha Na?

279
00:23:03,165 --> 00:23:04,652
Are you okay?

280
00:23:08,594 --> 00:23:10,294
Hey, Jung Woo Jae!

281
00:23:27,588 --> 00:23:29,063
Yoon Ha Na!

282
00:23:39,981 --> 00:23:41,821
I'm sorry, Jun Mo.

283
00:23:41,821 --> 00:23:44,746
Having to stop the production
a week after starting...

284
00:23:45,884 --> 00:23:49,321
I have no words to defend myself.

285
00:23:49,321 --> 00:23:52,894
It's fine. It's not like it was your fault.

286
00:23:52,894 --> 00:23:56,881
I spoke with the production company,
so don't worry about it.

287
00:23:56,881 --> 00:24:00,416
- Just focus on Ha Na's recovery.
- Thank you so much.

288
00:24:01,628 --> 00:24:04,954
Bad things have been happening to Ha Na lately.

289
00:24:04,954 --> 00:24:07,287
It's driving me mad, too.

290
00:24:07,287 --> 00:24:08,571
Oh, right.

291
00:24:08,571 --> 00:24:14,066
They even found toxic chemicals
in the banana milk Ha Na had in her fridge!

292
00:24:20,668 --> 00:24:22,525
Did you report it to the police?

293
00:24:22,525 --> 00:24:25,582
Well, they said they'd take care of it,

294
00:24:25,582 --> 00:24:27,876
but we still haven't heard back from them.

295
00:25:16,028 --> 00:25:19,788
[Great, let's proceed. I've paid up front.]
[Let me know when you're ready.]

296
00:25:26,994 --> 00:25:29,721
[Is there a problem?]

297
00:25:48,021 --> 00:25:50,698
Shut up for once!

298
00:26:16,782 --> 00:26:17,784
[Woo Jae's Father]

299
00:26:27,703 --> 00:26:30,834
Hello, sir. How are you doing?

300
00:26:41,518 --> 00:26:42,988
There you are.

301
00:26:45,049 --> 00:26:48,149
I changed the code,
and installed a new lock on the front door.

302
00:26:48,149 --> 00:26:50,133
They won't get back in here.

303
00:26:50,133 --> 00:26:51,857
Thank you, Woo Jae.

304
00:26:51,857 --> 00:26:53,569
You did well.

305
00:26:53,569 --> 00:26:55,240
It's nothing.

306
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:56,633
Are you okay?

307
00:26:58,994 --> 00:27:01,687
I have some business to see to.

308
00:27:01,687 --> 00:27:03,387
I'll leave you to it.

309
00:27:04,581 --> 00:27:06,095
Go on.

310
00:27:09,949 --> 00:27:11,986
- Shall we?
- Yeah.

311
00:27:14,476 --> 00:27:16,267
Look here! Look at me!

312
00:27:16,267 --> 00:27:18,863
Here, birdie, birdie!

313
00:27:18,863 --> 00:27:21,939
It's looking a bit limp.

314
00:27:24,223 --> 00:27:27,796
I assume you like this bird, Director Yang?

315
00:27:27,796 --> 00:27:30,423
I do. Pretty, isn't it?

316
00:27:30,423 --> 00:27:32,789
<i>- Ha Na.
- Yes?</i>

317
00:27:32,789 --> 00:27:35,089
- Cute.
<i>- Why don't we run somewhere far away?</i>

318
00:27:35,089 --> 00:27:36,540
<i>Run away?</i>

319
00:27:37,147 --> 00:27:40,243
We can go somewhere where nobody knows us,

320
00:27:40,243 --> 00:27:42,141
and live a life like any other.

321
00:27:42,743 --> 00:27:44,348
A normal life.

322
00:27:45,009 --> 00:27:46,743
A normal life?

323
00:27:46,743 --> 00:27:49,680
We'll wake up together in the morning,

324
00:27:49,680 --> 00:27:51,545
maybe bicker around,

325
00:27:51,545 --> 00:27:55,363
then by dinner, we'll share a beer and a laugh,

326
00:27:55,363 --> 00:27:57,463
and fall asleep together by night.

327
00:27:58,329 --> 00:28:01,729
A place where nobody knows
the global star Jung Woo Jae?

328
00:28:01,729 --> 00:28:03,952
Is that even a place on earth?

329
00:28:05,816 --> 00:28:07,189
I...

330
00:28:07,843 --> 00:28:09,840
don't have to be an actor.

331
00:28:17,296 --> 00:28:19,420
- What?
- I mean it.

332
00:28:19,420 --> 00:28:21,144
You're all I need.

333
00:28:21,144 --> 00:28:23,448
- Woo Jae.
- Emotional paralysis.

334
00:28:23,448 --> 00:28:26,479
It's caused by suppressing
your feelings, isn't it?

335
00:28:26,479 --> 00:28:30,247
I want you to laugh when you're happy,

336
00:28:30,247 --> 00:28:33,043
and get angry when you're sad.

337
00:28:33,043 --> 00:28:35,267
That's all I wish for.

338
00:28:35,267 --> 00:28:38,150
<i>I'm being serious, Ha Na.</i>

339
00:28:38,863 --> 00:28:41,807
I should've given you a call sooner, sir.

340
00:28:41,807 --> 00:28:45,152
I was just too busy, my apologies.

341
00:28:45,152 --> 00:28:47,700
Oh, we're way past
that stage of our friendship, I'm sure.

342
00:28:47,700 --> 00:28:49,544
You're working with my son.

343
00:28:49,544 --> 00:28:52,428
That means we're like family, doesn't it?

344
00:28:52,428 --> 00:28:54,243
I'm glad you think so.

345
00:28:54,243 --> 00:28:58,066
I'm always grateful for you, you know.

346
00:29:07,089 --> 00:29:08,929
<i>You should know when to stop.</i>

347
00:29:08,929 --> 00:29:10,629
<i>Don't ever reach out to me again.</i>

348
00:29:13,549 --> 00:29:16,183
<i>That ungrateful bastard...</i>

349
00:29:17,076 --> 00:29:18,376
<i>Hey, son!</i>

350
00:29:18,376 --> 00:29:20,774
<i>I'll call you later!</i>

351
00:29:30,123 --> 00:29:32,258
<i>Are you... Woo Jae's father?</i>

352
00:29:36,129 --> 00:29:38,580
<i>- Who...
- It's great to meet you.</i>

353
00:29:38,580 --> 00:29:41,103
<i>I'm Yang Jun Mo, a movie director.</i>

354
00:29:42,952 --> 00:29:44,504
<i>- Director Yang Jun Mo!
- Yes, sir.</i>

355
00:29:44,504 --> 00:29:47,283
<i>Director Yang! It's nice to meet you.</i>

356
00:29:47,923 --> 00:29:49,463
<i>Nice to meet you, sir.</i>

357
00:29:54,269 --> 00:29:55,993
It's nothing.

358
00:29:55,993 --> 00:29:58,724
My own darn son won't even answer my calls,

359
00:29:58,724 --> 00:30:02,773
but you check in on me,
and give me money as well.

360
00:30:03,476 --> 00:30:05,176
Of course I'm grateful.

361
00:30:06,083 --> 00:30:07,993
Hey, by the way.

362
00:30:07,993 --> 00:30:09,557
I heard the movie got canceled.

363
00:30:09,557 --> 00:30:12,168
- I heard you suffered some heavy losses.
- I'm alright.

364
00:30:12,168 --> 00:30:14,185
The actors' health comes first.

365
00:30:14,185 --> 00:30:17,103
In fact, I'm really enjoying my time off.

366
00:30:17,103 --> 00:30:19,653
It's nice that I have time to see you.

367
00:30:27,949 --> 00:30:31,670
Right, are you having any trouble recently?

368
00:30:37,150 --> 00:30:38,606
Well...

369
00:30:40,310 --> 00:30:41,708
Actually,

370
00:30:42,370 --> 00:30:45,048
can I borrow some money?

371
00:30:45,759 --> 00:30:50,369
- You know my kid will pay you back if I can't.
<i>- Alright, Woo Jae. Let's run away together.</i>

372
00:30:52,101 --> 00:30:53,607
Sir.

373
00:30:55,361 --> 00:30:58,038
I have a better idea.

374
00:31:04,508 --> 00:31:06,208
Alright, okay!

375
00:31:07,914 --> 00:31:11,974
I already took care of Ha Na's schedule,
so there's no need to worry.

376
00:31:11,974 --> 00:31:14,392
But things are different for Woo Jae.

377
00:31:14,392 --> 00:31:16,108
You can't leave straight away.

378
00:31:16,108 --> 00:31:18,628
I'll do my best to make it quick.

379
00:31:18,628 --> 00:31:22,616
But you still need to see your
pre-planned schedule through to the end.

380
00:31:23,255 --> 00:31:26,795
Of course. Thank you for understanding.

381
00:31:26,795 --> 00:31:28,685
Ye Rang,

382
00:31:28,685 --> 00:31:30,732
I have so much to thank you for.

383
00:31:32,188 --> 00:31:34,659
Well, you only wish to be happy.

384
00:31:34,659 --> 00:31:36,714
What else can I do?

385
00:31:37,316 --> 00:31:39,653
So, both of you,

386
00:31:39,653 --> 00:31:42,192
make sure that you end up happy.

387
00:31:42,192 --> 00:31:44,678
- Ye Rang...
- That's that, then!

388
00:31:44,678 --> 00:31:46,464
If you ever change your mind,

389
00:31:46,464 --> 00:31:48,542
and wish to return...

390
00:31:48,542 --> 00:31:50,555
just promise me.

391
00:31:51,344 --> 00:31:53,811
Promise to come back to me.

392
00:31:53,811 --> 00:31:55,382
Both of you.

393
00:31:55,382 --> 00:31:56,720
Yes.

394
00:31:58,516 --> 00:31:59,778
Good.

395
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:37,508
We'll start with the product name.

396
00:32:37,508 --> 00:32:40,632
Your right side looks best,
so we'll focus on that side.

397
00:32:40,632 --> 00:32:43,063
- Let's get ready.
- His left side is amazing, too.

398
00:32:43,063 --> 00:32:44,471
We'll get that side, too.

399
00:32:44,471 --> 00:32:46,243
Thank you.

400
00:32:46,243 --> 00:32:48,058
- This is perfect.
- Woo Jae.

401
00:32:48,058 --> 00:32:49,748
You look stunning today.

402
00:32:49,748 --> 00:32:51,179
- Really?
- Really.

403
00:32:51,179 --> 00:32:53,403
Could we touch up his makeup?

404
00:32:55,723 --> 00:32:57,743
Outsiders are prohibited!

405
00:32:57,743 --> 00:33:00,419
Hey, Woo Jae! It's your dad!

406
00:33:00,419 --> 00:33:01,887
What the hell.

407
00:33:01,887 --> 00:33:03,245
My boy.

408
00:33:03,245 --> 00:33:06,649
Your dad's weeping tears of blood from poverty,

409
00:33:06,649 --> 00:33:09,956
and you're frolicking around
posing for pictures?

410
00:33:10,615 --> 00:33:12,817
Sir, if you would just talk to me...

411
00:33:12,817 --> 00:33:15,237
- What's there to talk about?
- I'll take care of it.

412
00:33:15,237 --> 00:33:16,315
- Soo Hyuk!
- Yes!

413
00:33:16,315 --> 00:33:17,659
- Let's talk outside.
- Outside?

414
00:33:17,659 --> 00:33:19,830
- Let's go!
- What do you mean, "take care of?"

415
00:33:19,830 --> 00:33:23,284
Tell me how you're going to "take care of it!"

416
00:33:25,803 --> 00:33:29,331
<i>And you're frolicking around
posing for pictures?</i>

417
00:33:29,331 --> 00:33:32,524
[Is Jung Woo Jae a neglectful son?]
<i>Sir, if you would just talk to me...</i>

418
00:33:32,524 --> 00:33:33,944
<i>What's there to talk about?</i>

419
00:33:33,944 --> 00:33:35,831
<i>I'll take care of it.</i>

420
00:33:35,831 --> 00:33:36,871
<i>- Soo Hyuk!
- Yes!</i>

421
00:33:36,871 --> 00:33:38,155
<i>- Let's talk outside.
- Outside?</i>

422
00:33:38,155 --> 00:33:40,105
<i>- Let's go!
- What do you mean, "take care of?"</i>

423
00:33:40,105 --> 00:33:41,789
So this...

424
00:33:41,789 --> 00:33:44,659
didn't happen originally, right?

425
00:33:47,484 --> 00:33:49,184
Are you okay?

426
00:33:51,791 --> 00:33:53,114
Yeah.

427
00:34:06,043 --> 00:34:09,129
It was going to happen one day or another.

428
00:34:09,129 --> 00:34:11,904
I'm fine. Don't worry.

429
00:34:16,470 --> 00:34:19,201
[The grisly truth about the fan-favorite actor
Jung Woo Jae's childhood revealed?]

430
00:34:29,164 --> 00:34:31,863
Well, thanks to you...

431
00:34:31,863 --> 00:34:36,310
I got a pretty penny's worth of allowance
from my dear boy.

432
00:34:38,391 --> 00:34:40,815
It's nothing, sir.

433
00:34:40,815 --> 00:34:42,458
Woo Jae must've been surprised.

434
00:34:42,458 --> 00:34:44,158
Exactly, yeah.

435
00:34:45,918 --> 00:34:48,205
But...

436
00:34:48,205 --> 00:34:52,322
A person may seem like
some great artist to any observer,

437
00:34:52,322 --> 00:34:54,628
but people are all the same.

438
00:34:56,591 --> 00:34:57,972
Excuse me?

439
00:35:00,551 --> 00:35:02,962
I mean, you and I,

440
00:35:02,962 --> 00:35:04,619
we're the same scum of the earth.

441
00:35:04,619 --> 00:35:06,343
Don't you agree?

442
00:35:06,343 --> 00:35:08,314
Consider us equal from now on.

443
00:35:08,314 --> 00:35:12,135
I'd be glad to teach my son a lesson
every now and then.

444
00:35:13,838 --> 00:35:17,501
I don't understand what you mean.

445
00:35:27,511 --> 00:35:30,395
You think today's the only time I did this?

446
00:35:30,395 --> 00:35:33,809
<i>Woo Jae shouldn't have abandoned you like this.</i>

447
00:35:39,211 --> 00:35:42,375
<i>Woo Jae is shooting an advertisement tomorrow.</i>

448
00:35:42,375 --> 00:35:44,223
<i>Why don't you give him a visit?</i>

449
00:35:44,985 --> 00:35:48,292
<i>Teach him that he should
take better care of you.</i>

450
00:35:50,845 --> 00:35:53,052
<i>A fatherly life lesson, so to speak.</i>

451
00:35:58,364 --> 00:36:01,512
<i>Let me check the time.</i>

452
00:36:14,778 --> 00:36:17,069
You must've been frustrated about your movie.

453
00:36:17,069 --> 00:36:19,913
You wanted to screw my son over, didn't you?

454
00:36:19,913 --> 00:36:23,127
Isn't that why you paid me?

455
00:36:26,591 --> 00:36:29,830
I want you to have a pretty sum ready for me.

456
00:36:34,031 --> 00:36:38,215
And get some good whiskey,
like a Royal Ballantine's 30 years.

457
00:36:38,215 --> 00:36:40,997
My taste buds are sophisticated,
believe it or not.

458
00:36:42,191 --> 00:36:43,601
Got it?

459
00:36:43,601 --> 00:36:48,359
Serving me some darn crappy whiskey...

460
00:37:18,638 --> 00:37:22,261
<i>Sorry for the delay.
Are there any changes to the contract?</i>

461
00:37:29,731 --> 00:37:32,171
<i>Hey, Woo Jae! It's your dad!</i>

462
00:37:33,225 --> 00:37:35,284
<i>My boy.</i>

463
00:37:35,284 --> 00:37:37,239
<i>Your dad's weeping tears of blood from poverty,</i>

464
00:37:37,239 --> 00:37:38,965
[CEO Seo Ye Rang]

465
00:37:38,965 --> 00:37:42,259
<i>and you're frolicking around
posing for pictures?</i>

466
00:37:43,618 --> 00:37:46,102
Hi, CEO Seo.

467
00:37:46,102 --> 00:37:49,199
<i>Woo Jae and Ha Na
are with each other right now, right?</i>

468
00:37:49,199 --> 00:37:50,923
Yeah, why do you ask?

469
00:37:50,923 --> 00:37:53,106
<i>They're both not picking up.</i>

470
00:37:53,106 --> 00:37:54,538
<i>Just checking in.</i>

471
00:37:54,538 --> 00:37:56,631
<i>If they're together, that's fine.</i>

472
00:37:58,318 --> 00:38:00,425
Hey, you...

473
00:38:01,138 --> 00:38:03,695
Are you alright, Ye Rang?

474
00:38:03,695 --> 00:38:05,226
The company must be a mess, too.

475
00:38:05,226 --> 00:38:07,949
<i>Not the time to worry about me. I'm hanging up.</i>

476
00:38:14,951 --> 00:38:18,813
<i>If you don't want to ruin what we have now,</i>

477
00:38:18,813 --> 00:38:21,629
<i>then at least show me... a little respect.</i>

478
00:38:22,567 --> 00:38:24,322
Seo Ye Rang...

479
00:38:26,947 --> 00:38:28,854
[Han Soo Hyuk]

480
00:38:31,087 --> 00:38:32,318
<i>Hello?</i>

481
00:38:32,318 --> 00:38:34,222
- Hey, Soo Hyuk.
<i>- Yes?</i>

482
00:38:34,222 --> 00:38:37,666
I'm planning to
cook some burnt rice and braised beef.

483
00:38:37,666 --> 00:38:40,297
Could you take some over to CEO Seo?

484
00:38:40,297 --> 00:38:43,991
She can't stomach food when she's stressed.

485
00:38:43,991 --> 00:38:45,655
I just know she's starving herself again.

486
00:38:45,655 --> 00:38:48,258
<i>You're not wrong. But...</i>

487
00:38:48,258 --> 00:38:51,235
<i>Ye Rang's meeting up
with Kang Do Hoon for dinner today.</i>

488
00:38:51,235 --> 00:38:54,119
<i>He's acting really suspicious.</i>

489
00:38:54,119 --> 00:38:55,843
<i>Guess where they're meeting.</i>

490
00:38:55,843 --> 00:38:58,074
- Where?
<i>- Namsan Hotel!</i>

491
00:38:58,074 --> 00:38:59,758
<i>That's where they first met!</i>

492
00:38:59,758 --> 00:39:02,155
<i>I can feel it. He's going to propose!</i>

493
00:39:02,155 --> 00:39:03,964
He's... proposing?

494
00:39:10,378 --> 00:39:11,929
Nine years ago,

495
00:39:11,929 --> 00:39:14,766
I first met you here. And since then...

496
00:39:14,766 --> 00:39:17,896
my love for you has never changed.

497
00:39:18,858 --> 00:39:20,256
Do Hoon...

498
00:39:21,225 --> 00:39:25,311
Will you... marry me?

499
00:39:25,311 --> 00:39:27,869
All your past, and all your pain...

500
00:39:27,869 --> 00:39:29,858
I want to bear it for you.

501
00:39:29,858 --> 00:39:32,825
So that you never feel lonely
in this world we live in...

502
00:39:32,825 --> 00:39:34,525
I'll be there.

503
00:39:41,205 --> 00:39:42,528
Do Hoon.

504
00:40:14,511 --> 00:40:16,019
This...

505
00:40:16,798 --> 00:40:18,808
is my golden goose.

506
00:40:22,491 --> 00:40:24,765
Director Yang, I'm touched.

507
00:40:24,765 --> 00:40:27,806
You treat me so well.

508
00:40:42,431 --> 00:40:44,848
Are you goddamn kidding me?

509
00:40:47,898 --> 00:40:49,049
See this?

510
00:40:49,049 --> 00:40:51,806
What do you think would happen
if I leaked this to the press?

511
00:40:51,806 --> 00:40:54,097
Movie director Yang Jun Mo will be over.

512
00:40:54,097 --> 00:40:56,614
You'll fall to your demise in a heartbeat.

513
00:40:59,912 --> 00:41:01,639
I'm sure you have lots to lose.

514
00:41:01,639 --> 00:41:04,485
So why are you being so stingy?

515
00:41:06,225 --> 00:41:07,668
Sir.

516
00:41:08,859 --> 00:41:12,900
Do you know what I hate the most?

517
00:41:12,900 --> 00:41:14,304
What?

518
00:41:15,025 --> 00:41:17,385
- Mistakes.
- Mistakes?

519
00:41:17,385 --> 00:41:19,109
Yes.

520
00:41:19,109 --> 00:41:20,527
Well, I...

521
00:41:20,527 --> 00:41:23,449
I just can't stand the mistakes that I've made.

522
00:41:35,899 --> 00:41:38,021
You made your bed, now lie in it.

523
00:41:39,225 --> 00:41:41,529
If it's your mess,

524
00:41:41,529 --> 00:41:43,612
you should clean it up.

525
00:41:44,245 --> 00:41:46,075
Squeaky-clean.

526
00:41:56,432 --> 00:41:57,964
Exactly.

527
00:42:02,672 --> 00:42:04,372
You're right.

528
00:42:18,425 --> 00:42:20,530
I should clean it up.

529
00:42:22,525 --> 00:42:24,225
Squeaky-clean.

530
00:42:38,505 --> 00:42:40,376
Are you scared?

531
00:42:40,376 --> 00:42:42,100
It caught me by surprise.

532
00:42:42,100 --> 00:42:43,485
It's okay.

533
00:42:45,952 --> 00:42:48,761
I wish time would stop like this.

534
00:42:51,092 --> 00:42:52,577
Will we...

535
00:42:54,339 --> 00:42:56,423
really be okay?

536
00:42:57,372 --> 00:42:58,691
Yes.

537
00:42:59,705 --> 00:43:01,376
We'll be alright.

538
00:43:01,376 --> 00:43:03,214
Don't worry.

539
00:43:04,065 --> 00:43:05,356
You know me.

540
00:43:05,356 --> 00:43:07,277
I'm the Yoon Ha Na.

541
00:43:18,115 --> 00:43:19,365
[Dad]

542
00:43:19,365 --> 00:43:21,872
[Son]

543
00:43:37,626 --> 00:43:39,585
<i>The person you are calling is unavailable...</i>

544
00:43:39,585 --> 00:43:41,285
Not picking up?

545
00:43:42,879 --> 00:43:44,184
Yeah.

546
00:43:45,525 --> 00:43:47,598
I bet he's drinking.

547
00:44:02,079 --> 00:44:03,975
You made your bed...

548
00:44:04,959 --> 00:44:06,659
Now lie in it.

549
00:44:33,005 --> 00:44:35,312
<i>This is your last task.</i>

550
00:44:35,312 --> 00:44:37,888
<i>Make sure you make no mistakes.</i>

551
00:44:52,819 --> 00:44:54,989
Take a rest while I pack.

552
00:44:54,989 --> 00:44:56,892
I'll be quick.

553
00:44:56,892 --> 00:44:58,516
Our flight leaves in the early morning.
We have enough time.

554
00:44:58,516 --> 00:45:00,962
Take your time, and be careful.

555
00:45:04,905 --> 00:45:07,532
- I'll be back.
- Okay.

556
00:45:07,532 --> 00:45:09,169
- See you later.
- Stay inside.

557
00:45:09,169 --> 00:45:10,559
Okay.

558
00:45:23,701 --> 00:45:25,442
[Woo]

559
00:45:28,279 --> 00:45:31,585
Sorry, I fell asleep.

560
00:45:31,585 --> 00:45:33,010
Now?

561
00:45:34,339 --> 00:45:37,458
Yeah, I'm in the parking lot now.

562
00:45:38,132 --> 00:45:40,872
It's fine, I'll get there soon enough.

563
00:45:40,872 --> 00:45:43,199
Okay. Talk to you later.

564
00:45:46,352 --> 00:45:47,924
Ms. Yoon Ha Na.

565
00:47:11,639 --> 00:47:13,339
Jun Mo...

566
00:47:30,516 --> 00:47:32,303
Where were you running off to?

567
00:47:32,303 --> 00:47:34,220
Running away?

568
00:47:34,220 --> 00:47:36,797
Please, stop now.

569
00:47:36,797 --> 00:47:39,335
You're about to cross the point of no return.

570
00:47:39,335 --> 00:47:41,224
Tell me, why...

571
00:47:52,299 --> 00:47:54,279
It's all because of you.

572
00:47:54,279 --> 00:47:55,929
What?

573
00:47:55,929 --> 00:48:00,273
You came from the future
and messed with my movie, and my life.

574
00:48:00,273 --> 00:48:01,851
Do you have any idea...

575
00:48:01,851 --> 00:48:04,171
how long I've waited for you?

576
00:48:05,805 --> 00:48:07,654
Emotional paralysis?

577
00:48:09,132 --> 00:48:10,383
Leaving?

578
00:48:10,383 --> 00:48:12,256
Quitting acting?

579
00:48:18,732 --> 00:48:21,369
The camcorder is in my hands,

580
00:48:21,369 --> 00:48:23,877
yet you're still traveling through time. How?

581
00:48:32,319 --> 00:48:34,843
Isn't the camcorder the time machine?

582
00:48:34,843 --> 00:48:36,433
Or was it you all this time?

583
00:48:37,939 --> 00:48:40,222
Do I need to kill you to bring this to an end?

584
00:49:01,972 --> 00:49:04,490
Get it together, Yang Jun Mo.

585
00:49:12,492 --> 00:49:14,040
I'll...

586
00:49:14,692 --> 00:49:16,642
put an end to this.

587
00:49:18,732 --> 00:49:20,945
You're what made me do this.

588
00:49:22,565 --> 00:49:24,265
Don't blame me for it.

589
00:49:29,279 --> 00:49:32,689
The first thing you'll notice
is that you've lost your voice.

590
00:49:32,689 --> 00:49:36,171
Everything will become
an afterimage that'll last longer.

591
00:49:37,752 --> 00:49:41,290
This music, and my voice,
they'll all fade away.

592
00:49:41,290 --> 00:49:42,989
And slowly...

593
00:49:43,679 --> 00:49:47,128
you'll lose all feeling
in every fiber of your body.

594
00:49:49,012 --> 00:49:51,736
Finally, you'll forget how to breathe.

595
00:49:51,736 --> 00:49:53,973
It'll be a very deep,

596
00:49:53,973 --> 00:49:56,035
and peaceful sleep.

597
00:49:56,035 --> 00:49:58,939
Your heart will come to a quiet stop.

598
00:49:59,599 --> 00:50:01,003
What do you think?

599
00:50:01,003 --> 00:50:03,152
Sounds so serene, doesn't it?

600
00:50:14,232 --> 00:50:15,672
Ha Na!

601
00:50:19,525 --> 00:50:21,554
How did you find this place?

602
00:50:25,225 --> 00:50:28,169
<i>Are you sure you can do it?</i>

603
00:50:28,169 --> 00:50:31,720
<i>Don't question it.
If it's to save Ha Na and Woo Jae,</i>

604
00:50:31,720 --> 00:50:33,853
<i>what is there not to do?</i>

605
00:50:44,912 --> 00:50:46,323
<i>Okay.</i>

606
00:50:50,812 --> 00:50:53,509
<i>- I need to use the restroom.
- Sure, Jun Mo.</i>

607
00:50:53,509 --> 00:50:55,227
<i>Where's the toilet?</i>

608
00:50:55,227 --> 00:50:57,494
<i>I'll show you to it, sir.</i>

609
00:50:58,792 --> 00:51:00,769
<i>You're drunk, aren't you?</i>

610
00:51:00,769 --> 00:51:02,469
<i>You're hammered!</i>

611
00:51:03,439 --> 00:51:05,474
<i>Safe travels, Jun Mo!</i>

612
00:51:23,505 --> 00:51:25,539
<i>Come on, please work...</i>

613
00:51:31,372 --> 00:51:32,854
<i>It worked!</i>

614
00:51:45,668 --> 00:51:48,025
<i>Hey, Jun Mo!</i>

615
00:51:48,025 --> 00:51:49,759
<i>Are you drunk?</i>

616
00:51:52,299 --> 00:51:54,812
<i>Get over here, take a shot!</i>

617
00:51:54,812 --> 00:51:57,056
<i>You haven't changed, Seo Ye Rang.</i>

618
00:51:57,056 --> 00:51:58,867
<i>- You've still got it.
- Jun Mo.</i>

619
00:51:58,867 --> 00:52:00,497
<i>We're going full-out today.</i>

620
00:52:00,497 --> 00:52:02,959
<i>- Bottoms up.
- Bottoms up!</i>

621
00:52:21,167 --> 00:52:23,606
Is it done?

622
00:52:42,319 --> 00:52:43,812
Are you okay?

623
00:52:58,219 --> 00:52:59,668
What's this?

624
00:53:01,699 --> 00:53:03,213
You're crying.

625
00:53:06,992 --> 00:53:08,905
What the hell is this?

626
00:53:10,452 --> 00:53:12,829
What did you do to me?

627
00:53:15,232 --> 00:53:16,932
Did you lie to me?

628
00:53:34,965 --> 00:53:36,712
<i>What's your problem?</i>

629
00:53:36,712 --> 00:53:38,509
<i>- It's just nice to see you.
- Sure, me too.</i>

630
00:53:38,509 --> 00:53:40,347
<i>- Yeah, okay.
- Very nice, yeah.</i>

631
00:53:40,347 --> 00:53:42,491
<i>- Don't follow me.
- How are you doing these days?</i>

632
00:53:42,491 --> 00:53:45,073
<i>- I'm doing fine.
- I see...</i>

633
00:53:50,521 --> 00:53:52,452
<i>Okay.</i>

634
00:54:07,505 --> 00:54:08,879
<i>See here.</i>

635
00:54:08,879 --> 00:54:13,813
<i>Press this, and the light comes on.
That means it's on.</i>

636
00:54:13,813 --> 00:54:18,707
<i>Press it again, and the light turns off,
which means it's not listening in anymore.</i>

637
00:54:19,399 --> 00:54:21,329
<i>- Feel free to make use of it.
- Okay.</i>

638
00:54:21,329 --> 00:54:23,240
<i>Think of it as your own.</i>

639
00:54:23,240 --> 00:54:25,443
<i>- Thank you.
- Got it.</i>

640
00:54:28,852 --> 00:54:30,943
<i>- Try it out.
- Okay.</i>

641
00:54:30,943 --> 00:54:32,420
<i>This... emotional paralysis.</i>

642
00:54:32,420 --> 00:54:34,853
<i>Is it possible to act it out?</i>

643
00:54:34,853 --> 00:54:38,304
<i>My concern, exactly.
Your temper is one to behold.</i>

644
00:54:38,304 --> 00:54:40,088
<i>- It won't be easy to fake it.
- Hey.</i>

645
00:54:40,088 --> 00:54:41,872
<i>This is Yoon Ha Na we're talking about.</i>

646
00:54:41,872 --> 00:54:43,596
<i>She's good, you know.</i>

647
00:54:43,596 --> 00:54:46,171
<i>She already secured a diagnosis.</i>

648
00:55:11,632 --> 00:55:14,456
<i>Emotional... paralysis?</i>

649
00:55:15,105 --> 00:55:16,529
<i>What's that?</i>

650
00:55:16,529 --> 00:55:21,017
<i>My brain can't process emotions like
happiness, sadness, and even surprise.</i>

651
00:55:21,017 --> 00:55:23,458
<i>It has a delayed response to feelings.</i>

652
00:55:32,014 --> 00:55:33,867
[Banana milk]

653
00:55:41,907 --> 00:55:43,198
<i>Ha Na!</i>

654
00:55:43,198 --> 00:55:44,842
<i>- Ha Na!
- What, what is it?</i>

655
00:55:44,842 --> 00:55:46,542
<i>What's wrong, Ha Na?</i>

656
00:55:48,221 --> 00:55:49,805
<i>Hey, Jung Woo Jae.</i>

657
00:55:51,387 --> 00:55:52,951
<i>- Call emergency services.
- Okay!</i>

658
00:55:52,951 --> 00:55:54,420
<i>My phone...</i>

659
00:55:58,881 --> 00:56:00,581
<i>The wiretap!</i>

660
00:56:24,174 --> 00:56:26,609
You can't do this.

661
00:56:45,587 --> 00:56:47,147
No...

662
00:56:47,147 --> 00:56:48,847
No!

663
00:56:51,327 --> 00:56:52,789
No...

664
00:56:54,761 --> 00:56:56,205
Stop whining.

665
00:56:56,205 --> 00:56:57,905
It's just saline.

666
00:57:05,327 --> 00:57:07,381
<i>Hi, Park Gi Tae.</i>

667
00:57:07,381 --> 00:57:09,347
<i>So we meet again.</i>

668
00:57:09,347 --> 00:57:11,047
<i>Nice to see you, Park Gi Tae.</i>

669
00:57:14,781 --> 00:57:16,481
<i>Hey, Yoon Ha Ru!</i>

670
00:57:55,521 --> 00:57:57,111
<i>Yoon Ha Ru...</i>

671
00:57:58,541 --> 00:57:59,997
<i>Sorry.</i>

672
00:58:03,621 --> 00:58:05,162
<i>Are you okay?</i>

673
00:58:05,162 --> 00:58:06,662
<i>I'm fine.</i>

674
00:58:40,701 --> 00:58:42,887
<i>You're a good fighter, Woo Jae.</i>

675
00:58:45,307 --> 00:58:47,625
<i>This is a problem.</i>

676
00:58:47,625 --> 00:58:53,046
<i>It seems that Mr. Gi Tae will take the blame
for Jun Mo's crimes if we let this play out.</i>

677
00:58:53,046 --> 00:58:56,947
<i>Aggravated intimidation and attempted murder...</i>

678
00:58:56,947 --> 00:58:59,825
<i>That'll land you in jail for at least 20 years,
or even a life sentence.</i>

679
00:58:59,825 --> 00:59:01,255
<i>What a shame.</i>

680
00:59:01,862 --> 00:59:02,991
<i>But...</i>

681
00:59:02,991 --> 00:59:04,609
<i>If you cooperate with us,</i>

682
00:59:04,609 --> 00:59:07,353
<i>I'll fabricate a mitigating factor
to reduce your sentence.</i>

683
00:59:07,353 --> 00:59:12,634
<i>If the jury likes what they hear,
you may be freed way sooner than you'd expect.</i>

684
00:59:12,634 --> 00:59:14,345
<i>How does that sound?</i>

685
00:59:14,345 --> 00:59:16,054
<i>Park Gi Tae.</i>

686
00:59:16,054 --> 00:59:18,351
<i>If you help us out this once,</i>

687
00:59:18,351 --> 00:59:20,107
<i>you can start anew.</i>

688
00:59:20,107 --> 00:59:23,651
<i>Or you can face the full consequences
of all your previous murders and attempts,</i>

689
00:59:23,651 --> 00:59:27,522
<i>and take the bullet
for Jun Mo just to rot in jail.</i>

690
00:59:27,522 --> 00:59:29,399
<i>Don't even think about running away.</i>

691
00:59:29,399 --> 00:59:31,967
<i>We'll find you anyway
if we put our minds to it.</i>

692
00:59:31,967 --> 00:59:34,185
<i>You seem like a good guy, come on. Stand up.</i>

693
00:59:34,185 --> 00:59:37,008
<i>It's okay, stand up. Up, boy, up.</i>

694
00:59:37,667 --> 00:59:39,582
<i>That's better.</i>

695
00:59:55,804 --> 00:59:58,038
<i>I'm sure you already know...</i>

696
00:59:58,038 --> 01:00:00,458
<i>what you have to do.</i>

697
01:00:09,714 --> 01:00:11,610
You guys are...

698
01:00:12,321 --> 01:00:14,737
absolutely oblivious, aren't you?

699
01:00:17,447 --> 01:00:19,647
I'm the one...

700
01:00:20,374 --> 01:00:24,960
who saved you from the vermin of this world,
the lowest of the low!

701
01:00:24,960 --> 01:00:27,526
I did that!

702
01:00:28,457 --> 01:00:31,304
I'm the good guy, the protector of the story.

703
01:00:31,304 --> 01:00:33,848
You're delusional, Yang Jun Mo.

704
01:00:35,237 --> 01:00:37,555
The good guy? The protector?

705
01:00:37,555 --> 01:00:40,985
Stop trying to make it sound pretty,
and face the truth.

706
01:00:40,985 --> 01:00:43,396
You didn't save anyone.

707
01:00:43,396 --> 01:00:45,207
You didn't create art.

708
01:00:45,207 --> 01:00:48,324
It's just your pathetic possessiveness...

709
01:00:48,324 --> 01:00:50,024
and obsession.

710
01:00:51,344 --> 01:00:55,675
Humans can never become a god.

711
01:00:55,675 --> 01:00:58,399
So just stop this,

712
01:00:58,399 --> 01:01:00,725
and wake up from your delusions of grandeur.

713
01:01:04,017 --> 01:01:06,479
Protect yourself first.

714
01:01:06,479 --> 01:01:08,240
No.

715
01:01:08,240 --> 01:01:10,164
I'm different.

716
01:01:10,164 --> 01:01:14,111
I'm your savior,
you imperfect and flawed creatures.

717
01:01:14,111 --> 01:01:15,635
Delusions of grandeur?

718
01:01:15,635 --> 01:01:17,212
No.

719
01:01:17,212 --> 01:01:20,113
This is artistry, nearing perfection.

720
01:01:21,751 --> 01:01:25,508
You're worth nothing outside of my frame.

721
01:01:25,508 --> 01:01:28,048
You're over without me.

722
01:01:29,031 --> 01:01:30,435
You're the one who's over.

723
01:01:30,435 --> 01:01:32,427
Nonsense!

724
01:01:34,591 --> 01:01:36,972
The ending that you made...

725
01:01:39,517 --> 01:01:41,398
Aren't you curious?

726
01:01:56,631 --> 01:01:58,331
<i>There we are.</i>

727
01:02:00,744 --> 01:02:03,432
<i>- The quality is surprisingly good.
- Sure is.</i>

728
01:02:08,571 --> 01:02:11,352
<i>- Is it showing up well?
- Yeah, look at this.</i>

729
01:02:13,244 --> 01:02:14,944
<i>It's pretty clear, right?</i>

730
01:02:20,497 --> 01:02:22,072
<i>This is it.</i>

731
01:02:22,072 --> 01:02:24,669
[What a creep, can't believe I liked his movies]
[That's not love, absolutely vile!]

732
01:02:24,669 --> 01:02:26,246
[I just saw the video, I'm shaking!]
[Is this real?]

733
01:02:26,246 --> 01:02:28,173
[Is this what he meant by "muse?"]
[I'm so creeped out I can't sleep!]

734
01:02:31,557 --> 01:02:33,581
It's over now.

735
01:02:44,885 --> 01:02:46,154
No.

736
01:03:04,491 --> 01:03:06,191
Yang Jun Mo!

737
01:03:08,624 --> 01:03:10,465
Stay back.

738
01:03:21,577 --> 01:03:23,657
You've ruined me.

739
01:03:23,657 --> 01:03:24,835
Yang Jun Mo.

740
01:03:24,835 --> 01:03:26,619
Give up and pay for your crimes.

741
01:03:26,619 --> 01:03:29,196
And keep on living, but properly this time.

742
01:03:29,196 --> 01:03:30,896
Such a tragedy.

743
01:03:31,624 --> 01:03:34,660
Mere creations, betraying the creator...

744
01:03:35,344 --> 01:03:37,448
You've wrought this hell with your own hands.

745
01:03:37,448 --> 01:03:40,908
- Stop this, Yang Jun Mo.
- I'll decide my own fate.

746
01:03:43,491 --> 01:03:45,488
I'm leaving this hellhole.

747
01:03:45,488 --> 01:03:48,025
If you jump now,

748
01:03:48,025 --> 01:03:50,883
what will the world remember you as?

749
01:03:50,883 --> 01:03:55,004
You won't be the ingenious movie director
Yang Jun Mo, but a criminal.

750
01:03:55,004 --> 01:04:00,135
Or maybe you'll be Yang Jun Mo,
history's most pathetic director.

751
01:04:00,871 --> 01:04:04,848
Is that... what you've dreamt of?

752
01:04:06,124 --> 01:04:08,171
You know it isn't.

753
01:04:41,084 --> 01:04:43,141
Come down with us.

754
01:04:43,141 --> 01:04:44,702
Jun Mo.

755
01:05:33,177 --> 01:05:34,877
Stand back!

756
01:05:38,124 --> 01:05:40,161
If you hadn't abandoned my world...

757
01:05:40,161 --> 01:05:42,439
If you hadn't abandoned me...

758
01:05:42,439 --> 01:05:45,089
If not only for that damn camcorder!

759
01:05:45,089 --> 01:05:47,160
This is all your fault, Yoon Ha Na.

760
01:05:47,160 --> 01:05:48,860
Die!

761
01:05:50,511 --> 01:05:52,211
Ha Na!

762
01:05:57,664 --> 01:05:59,948
<i>See, judo is all about aura.</i>

763
01:05:59,948 --> 01:06:03,091
<i>Once you get a grip,
you use your "you're dead meat" stare.</i>

764
01:06:50,891 --> 01:06:55,641
<i>Police have referred Mr. Yang, the suspect
charged with attempted murder of actress Yoon,</i>

765
01:06:55,641 --> 01:06:58,785
<i>to prosecution this morning.</i>

766
01:06:58,785 --> 01:07:02,903
<i>The chilling truth uncovered
about Korea's most well-known film director</i>

767
01:07:02,903 --> 01:07:06,391
<i>has plunged the nation into shock and chaos.</i>

768
01:07:06,391 --> 01:07:08,521
<i>Moreover, the investigation of the crime scene</i>

769
01:07:08,521 --> 01:07:13,772
<i>led to the discovery of the body of a John Doe
with severely damaged fingerprints and teeth,</i>

770
01:07:13,772 --> 01:07:16,036
<i>signaling that the case
is more than an attempt,</i>

771
01:07:16,036 --> 01:07:20,020
<i>and will be treated
as a serial violent crime case.</i>

772
01:07:20,020 --> 01:07:23,464
<i>With past crimes being uncovered
on top of the attempted murder,</i>

773
01:07:23,464 --> 01:07:29,015
<i>experts speculate that he will not be able to
escape a heavy sentence.</i>

774
01:07:29,015 --> 01:07:32,965
<i>The prosecution will focus heavily
on the deliberate nature of the crime</i>

775
01:07:32,965 --> 01:07:37,975
<i>and the defendant's tendency
to reoffend in this trial.</i>

776
01:07:50,397 --> 01:07:53,017
I've been wondering something.

777
01:07:53,017 --> 01:07:55,264
Can I ask you a question?

778
01:07:55,264 --> 01:07:56,876
What is it?

779
01:07:57,504 --> 01:07:59,088
Tae Kang...

780
01:07:59,088 --> 01:08:01,156
You mean Do Hoon oppa?

781
01:08:01,156 --> 01:08:03,217
"Oppa?"

782
01:08:03,217 --> 01:08:05,589
Calling everyone "oppa" all willy-nilly...

783
01:08:09,771 --> 01:08:12,865
The proposal...

784
01:08:13,837 --> 01:08:17,637
Did you... say yes?

785
01:08:17,637 --> 01:08:19,800
How do you know about this?

786
01:08:22,377 --> 01:08:23,869
Just...

787
01:08:50,011 --> 01:08:51,986
<i>I saw that coming.</i>

788
01:08:53,217 --> 01:08:56,068
<i>But it still hurts to be rejected.</i>

789
01:08:57,444 --> 01:08:59,297
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

790
01:08:59,297 --> 01:09:01,797
<i>Your feelings are too valuable
to get hurt like this.</i>

791
01:09:04,837 --> 01:09:07,824
<i>I was too late in realizing this, but...</i>

792
01:09:07,824 --> 01:09:09,524
<i>Yoon Ha Ru.</i>

793
01:09:10,591 --> 01:09:13,118
<i>He's not my past, but still my present.</i>

794
01:09:15,784 --> 01:09:17,302
Then...

795
01:09:18,531 --> 01:09:19,918
What?

796
01:09:20,931 --> 01:09:25,341
That means I'm not your past, but your present.

797
01:09:25,341 --> 01:09:28,119
So I still have a chance...

798
01:09:28,119 --> 01:09:29,819
Right?

799
01:09:31,557 --> 01:09:35,168
What if... you do?

800
01:09:39,204 --> 01:09:41,949
It's hard to explain,

801
01:09:42,761 --> 01:09:45,691
but I can tell you one thing.

802
01:09:45,691 --> 01:09:47,980
Any time spent without you...

803
01:09:48,637 --> 01:09:50,788
has no meaning at all to me.

804
01:09:56,153 --> 01:09:58,501
You may not know,

805
01:09:59,391 --> 01:10:02,024
but my past has been Seo Ye Rang,

806
01:10:03,957 --> 01:10:07,508
and every bit of the present
that I have left in the future,

807
01:10:07,508 --> 01:10:09,208
all of it,

808
01:10:09,977 --> 01:10:11,677
is you, Seo Ye Rang.

809
01:10:18,231 --> 01:10:20,131
Come back to me.

810
01:10:21,871 --> 01:10:24,201
I won't make you feel lonely.

811
01:10:24,201 --> 01:10:26,257
I won't keep you waiting.

812
01:10:26,877 --> 01:10:28,465
I promise...

813
01:10:29,071 --> 01:10:33,064
I'll be your boss... this time.

814
01:11:15,097 --> 01:11:17,124
It's been hard, hasn't it?

815
01:11:19,437 --> 01:11:21,410
I'm sorry.

816
01:11:21,410 --> 01:11:23,250
And thank you.

817
01:11:26,448 --> 01:11:28,711
I should've confessed first.

818
01:11:30,217 --> 01:11:32,721
I could've had all this happiness,

819
01:11:32,721 --> 01:11:35,619
but I was scared to tell you that I love you.

820
01:11:35,619 --> 01:11:37,520
All that needless struggling...

821
01:11:42,597 --> 01:11:44,108
I like you.

822
01:11:44,108 --> 01:11:45,452
Woo Jae.

823
01:11:45,452 --> 01:11:49,204
I like you so, so much.

824
01:11:51,704 --> 01:11:54,748
I love you, Ha Na.

825
01:11:54,748 --> 01:11:56,257
I love you more.

826
01:11:59,215 --> 01:12:02,179
No, I think my love is bigger.

827
01:12:02,179 --> 01:12:04,788
Alright. Whatever you say.

828
01:12:11,015 --> 01:12:14,793
You know what the most cruel part of it was?

829
01:12:16,862 --> 01:12:19,007
The moment I lost you...

830
01:12:20,142 --> 01:12:23,578
all the emotions that I had lost
came flooding back.

831
01:12:25,209 --> 01:12:28,429
You always manage to save me, in whatever way.

832
01:12:30,422 --> 01:12:32,066
But now,

833
01:12:32,066 --> 01:12:33,986
you've saved me.

834
01:12:40,275 --> 01:12:42,846
I was crying so hard when you saved me.

835
01:12:42,846 --> 01:12:44,950
You know what you said?

836
01:12:45,669 --> 01:12:47,046
What?

837
01:12:47,046 --> 01:12:50,141
You saw me cry and said, "Thank goodness."

838
01:12:50,141 --> 01:12:51,572
Dummy.

839
01:12:54,102 --> 01:12:56,831
I may be a dummy, but I'm still happy.

840
01:12:58,069 --> 01:12:59,898
Don't hurt.

841
01:13:00,829 --> 01:13:02,529
And don't get hurt, either.

842
01:13:03,369 --> 01:13:05,069
Promise me.

843
01:13:07,422 --> 01:13:09,345
You promise me, too.

844
01:13:34,482 --> 01:13:36,988
<i>The camcorder disappeared,</i>

845
01:13:40,929 --> 01:13:46,160
<i>and our summer that seemed unending
had come to an end.</i>

846
01:13:54,415 --> 01:13:57,287
<i>There was no more time traveling,</i>

847
01:13:57,927 --> 01:14:00,951
<i>but we were together.</i>

848
01:14:40,642 --> 01:14:44,835
<i>Could everything have been a gift from god?</i>

849
01:14:44,835 --> 01:14:51,326
<i>As for why we were granted
such miracles, it's still a mystery.</i>

850
01:14:52,035 --> 01:14:53,946
<i>But we came to the realization</i>

851
01:14:53,946 --> 01:14:57,877
<i>that our hands, intertwined, and this warmth...</i>

852
01:14:57,877 --> 01:15:02,553
<i>is the grandest magic of all,
protecting each other.</i>

853
01:15:04,269 --> 01:15:11,503
The Best Actress Award of the
31st Baekryong Film Awards, 2027,

854
01:15:13,689 --> 01:15:15,019
goes to...

855
01:15:15,019 --> 01:15:19,057
Yoon Ha Na, from
"Every day with Yesterday's Miracle."

856
01:15:19,057 --> 01:15:21,184
Congratulations!

857
01:15:31,469 --> 01:15:35,120
Yoon Ha Na, as Yoon Mi Gyeong

858
01:15:35,120 --> 01:15:37,577
in Director Na's film,
"Every day with Yesterday's Miracle,"

859
01:15:37,577 --> 01:15:41,008
had skillfully transformed human sadness
into a dazzling sense of liveliness,

860
01:15:41,008 --> 01:15:44,596
receiving countless compliments
about her astonishing proficiency.

861
01:15:44,596 --> 01:15:48,736
She had endured a long time
acting in nameless, short-lived roles.

862
01:15:48,736 --> 01:15:53,747
The silent journey that she had taken,
and her seemingly endless passion for acting

863
01:15:53,747 --> 01:15:58,779
make today's award an even more valuable one.

864
01:16:02,163 --> 01:16:04,069
Thank you so much.

865
01:16:05,323 --> 01:16:07,023
So this is...

866
01:16:09,383 --> 01:16:12,469
what it feels like.

867
01:16:14,889 --> 01:16:19,620
I'm thankful for the tears that I'm shedding,

868
01:16:19,620 --> 01:16:22,233
and I feel blessed tonight.

869
01:16:30,136 --> 01:16:34,944
I have always learned the world
by living through my roles.

870
01:16:34,944 --> 01:16:37,201
That's how I grew.

871
01:16:37,860 --> 01:16:40,473
This role was no exception to that.

872
01:16:42,323 --> 01:16:44,916
Yoon Mi Gyeong and Yoon Ha Na...

873
01:16:45,716 --> 01:16:49,251
had a lot in common, luckily for me.

874
01:16:51,049 --> 01:16:54,307
They both had been broken

875
01:16:54,307 --> 01:16:59,911
from trying to ignore the emotions
that would come crashing toward them.

876
01:17:01,796 --> 01:17:06,460
They both had failed to see the miracles
that they already had,

877
01:17:07,209 --> 01:17:10,852
and had been fooled by the false concept
of "a better future,"

878
01:17:11,489 --> 01:17:14,262
coveting an unattainable miracle.

879
01:17:15,356 --> 01:17:17,760
All that time spent,

880
01:17:17,760 --> 01:17:20,363
hurting not only others,

881
01:17:20,363 --> 01:17:23,599
but myself as well...

882
01:17:23,599 --> 01:17:28,903
Living Mi Gyeong's and my days,

883
01:17:29,586 --> 01:17:31,870
I finally opened my eyes.

884
01:17:31,870 --> 01:17:34,674
I'm living in a world
where I wake up every day...

885
01:17:39,313 --> 01:17:42,600
to the breath of my loved one,

886
01:17:43,823 --> 01:17:46,359
and I'm allowed to share that moment.

887
01:17:47,063 --> 01:17:49,529
I can hold their hands,

888
01:17:50,156 --> 01:17:53,458
and talk about the little things in life.

889
01:17:55,349 --> 01:17:58,219
That bit of warmth,
so easily taken for granted,

890
01:17:58,882 --> 01:18:03,500
is the miracle of your every day,
happening so close by.

891
01:18:04,316 --> 01:18:05,796
Please,

892
01:18:05,796 --> 01:18:09,549
I hope for all of you to discover your miracle,

893
01:18:09,549 --> 01:18:11,987
and to love it wholeheartedly.

894
01:18:11,987 --> 01:18:15,224
We, having endured countless yesterdays,

895
01:18:15,224 --> 01:18:18,349
to finally meet our today,

896
01:18:18,349 --> 01:18:21,065
are already the glorious miracles.

897
01:18:21,793 --> 01:18:24,487
I hope you never forget that.

898
01:18:27,177 --> 01:18:29,074
Thank you.

899
01:18:57,483 --> 01:18:58,974
Ha Na.

900
01:18:59,563 --> 01:19:01,287
Yeah?

901
01:19:01,287 --> 01:19:03,883
What... do you dream of?

902
01:19:03,883 --> 01:19:05,656
My dream?

903
01:19:05,656 --> 01:19:07,229
That's sudden.

904
01:19:10,497 --> 01:19:12,643
All of them have already come true.

905
01:19:14,510 --> 01:19:18,180
I'm with you right now, aren't I?

906
01:19:20,490 --> 01:19:21,876
What about you?

907
01:19:25,570 --> 01:19:27,001
I don't know.

908
01:19:27,001 --> 01:19:29,125
What could I possibly dream of?

909
01:19:29,125 --> 01:19:30,609
I have no clue.

910
01:19:30,609 --> 01:19:33,115
What could you possibly dream of?

911
01:19:33,963 --> 01:19:37,236
<i>What about after your dream comes true?
What do you want to do then?</i>

912
01:19:37,236 --> 01:19:41,302
<i>What do you think you'd want to do the most?</i>

913
01:19:42,570 --> 01:19:44,330
Ha Na.

914
01:19:44,330 --> 01:19:45,617
Yes?

915
01:20:18,810 --> 01:20:20,510
I dream of...

916
01:20:21,797 --> 01:20:23,270
you.

917
01:20:24,110 --> 01:20:25,613
Ha Na,

918
01:20:28,237 --> 01:20:29,937
will you...

919
01:20:31,017 --> 01:20:33,029
be mine, forever?

920
01:21:59,150 --> 01:22:00,909
Hey, kiddos.

921
01:22:00,909 --> 01:22:03,891
If you're ever lost, you can ask me.

922
01:22:05,637 --> 01:22:07,677
Ta-da!

923
01:22:08,737 --> 01:22:10,141
What?

924
01:22:13,470 --> 01:22:14,641
Babe?

925
01:22:14,641 --> 01:22:19,569
Ha Na's ring...
is so big and pretty, don't you think?

926
01:22:20,650 --> 01:22:24,334
You know my love for you
is bigger than some diamond!

927
01:22:24,334 --> 01:22:27,191
Then make up for it by making me breakfast
every day for the rest of our lives.

928
01:22:27,191 --> 01:22:28,429
- Sure!
- Really?

929
01:22:28,429 --> 01:22:29,986
Of course!

930
01:22:29,986 --> 01:22:31,883
So cute!

931
01:22:31,883 --> 01:22:33,281
Anyway, Woo Jae,

932
01:22:33,281 --> 01:22:36,331
are you sure you can handle her?

933
01:22:36,331 --> 01:22:38,031
Of course I can.

934
01:22:39,617 --> 01:22:42,202
Hey, both of you, cut it out!

935
01:22:42,202 --> 01:22:44,370
Stop it, I'm starving.

936
01:22:44,370 --> 01:22:46,236
- Let's get something to eat.
- Really?

937
01:22:46,236 --> 01:22:47,565
You should pay.

938
01:23:04,643 --> 01:23:08,221
[If you have someone who,
in your eyes, lights up the world,]

939
01:23:10,572 --> 01:23:14,614
[tell them how much you love them
before it's too late.]

940
01:23:16,151 --> 01:23:19,631
[Your today is too bright
to harbor any hesitation.]
